### Description
This Terraform program sets up a Route 53 hosted zone named "main" and configures weighted routing policies to distribute traffic between a primary database instance and two replica database instances. The primary instance will receive 40% of the traffic, while each replica will receive 30%.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "main_zone" {
  name = "main"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "primary_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.main_zone.zone_id
  name    = "db.main"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300

  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 40
  }

  records = ["192.168.1.1"]  # Replace with actual IP address of primary DB instance
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "replica_1_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.main_zone.zone_id
  name    = "db.main"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300

  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 30
  }

  records = ["192.168.1.2"]  # Replace with actual IP address of replica-1 DB instance
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "replica_2_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.main_zone.zone_id
  name    = "db.main"
  type    = "A"
  ttl     = 300

  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 30
  }

  records = ["192.168.1.3"]  # Replace with actual IP address of replica-2 DB instance
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **Route 53 Hosted Zone**: A Route 53 hosted zone named "main" is created.
- **Route 53 Records**: Three Route 53 records are created for the primary and two replica database instances:
  - `primary_record`: Configured with a weighted routing policy of 40.
  - `replica_1_record`: Configured with a weighted routing policy of 30.
  - `replica_2_record`: Configured with a weighted routing policy of 30.
- **IP Addresses**: Placeholder IP addresses (`192.168.1.1`, `192.168.1.2`, `192.168.1.3`) are used for the database instances. These should be replaced with the actual IP addresses of your database instances.

