### Description
This Terraform program creates an Elastic Beanstalk application along with an IAM role and a configuration template. The IAM role is necessary for managing the lifecycle of application versions in Elastic Beanstalk. The configuration template can be used to define settings for environments created from this application.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "beanstalk_service_role" {
  name = "elastic-beanstalk-service-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticbeanstalk.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkEnhancedHealth",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkWebTier",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSElasticBeanstalkWorkerTier"
  ]
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "elastic_beanstalk_app" {
  name        = "my-elastic-beanstalk-app"
  description = "My Elastic Beanstalk Application"

  appversion_lifecycle {
    service_role = aws_iam_role.beanstalk_service_role.arn
    max_count    = 12
    max_age_in_days = 365
    delete_source_from_s3 = true
  }
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_configuration_template" "elastic_beanstalk_template" {
  name        = "my-elastic-beanstalk-template"
  application = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.elastic_beanstalk_app.name
  description = "My Elastic Beanstalk Configuration Template"

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:autoscaling:launchconfiguration"
    name      = "InstanceType"
    value     = "t3.micro"
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:ec2:vpc"
    name      = "VPCId"
    value     = "vpc-12345678"  # Replace with a valid VPC ID
  }

  setting {
    namespace = "aws:ec2:vpc"
    name      = "Subnets"
    value     = "subnet-12345678,subnet-87654321"  # Replace with valid subnet IDs
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `elastic-beanstalk-service-role` is created with policies necessary for Elastic Beanstalk operations.
3. **Elastic Beanstalk Application**: An Elastic Beanstalk application named `my-elastic-beanstalk-app` is created. It includes an `appversion_lifecycle` block that specifies the IAM role for managing application versions, along with settings for maximum count and age of versions and whether to delete source files from S3.
4. **Elastic Beanstalk Configuration Template**: A configuration template named `my-elastic-beanstalk-template` is created, linked to the Elastic Beanstalk application. It includes settings for the instance type, VPC ID, and subnets. Replace the placeholder VPC and subnet IDs with valid values from your AWS account.

