### Description
This Terraform program sets up a non-alias AWS Route 53 record linked to a private Route 53 zone named "internal.example53.com". The private zone is associated with an AWS VPC named "main". The program ensures that the VPC is properly configured with DNS settings as required.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Default region, can be changed as needed
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
  tags = {
    Name = "main"
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "private_zone" {
  name = "internal.example53.com"
  vpc {
    vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id
  }
  tags = {
    Name = "private_zone"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Sets up the AWS provider with a default region (`us-west-2`).
2. Creates an AWS VPC named "main" with a CIDR block of `10.0.0.0/16` and enables DNS support and hostnames.
3. Creates a private Route 53 zone named "internal.example53.com" and associates it with the "main" VPC.

