### Description
The Terraform program defined below creates a basic Route53 traffic policy using the AWS provider. The traffic policy is named "example_traffic_policy" and includes a simple document that defines a weighted routing policy. This configuration ensures that the traffic policy can be deployed in any AWS region, with a default region of "us-east-1".

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_route53_traffic_policy" "example_traffic_policy" {
  name    = "example_traffic_policy"
  comment = "Example traffic policy for weighted routing"

  document = jsonencode({
    AWSPolicyFormatVersion = "2015-10-01"
    RecordType             = "A"
    StartEndpoint          = "my_endpoint"

    Endpoints = {
      my_endpoint = {
        Type = "WEIGHTED"
        WeightedRoutingConfig = {
          Weight = 100
        }
      }
    }
  })
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up a Route53 traffic policy with a weighted routing configuration. The policy is named "example_traffic_policy" and includes a comment for clarity. The `document` attribute contains a JSON-encoded policy document that specifies the routing behavior. In this example, the policy routes all traffic to a single endpoint with a weight of 100.

