### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster with the specified node type (`dax.r4.large`) and replication factor (`1`). The program also sets up the necessary dependencies, including an IAM role, a subnet group, and a parameter group, to ensure the DAX cluster can be successfully provisioned.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_role" {
  name = "dax-cluster-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "dax_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonDAXFullAccess"
}

resource "aws_dax_subnet_group" "dax_subnet_group" {
  name       = "dax-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
}

resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "dax_parameter_group" {
  name   = "dax-parameter-group"
  family = "DAX 1.0"

  parameters {
    name  = "parameter_name"
    value = "parameter_value"
  }
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster_example" {
  cluster_name         = "dax-cluster-example"
  iam_role_arn         = aws_iam_role.dax_role.arn
  node_type            = "dax.r4.large"
  replication_factor   = 1
  subnet_group_name    = aws_dax_subnet_group.dax_subnet_group.name
  parameter_group_name = aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_parameter_group.name

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role.dax_role,
    aws_dax_subnet_group.dax_subnet_group,
    aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_parameter_group
  ]
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `dax-cluster-role` is created with a trust policy allowing DAX to assume the role. The `AmazonDAXFullAccess` policy is attached to this role.
- **DAX Subnet Group**: A subnet group named `dax-subnet-group` is created with two example subnet IDs. Replace these with actual subnet IDs from your VPC.
- **DAX Parameter Group**: A parameter group named `dax-parameter-group` is created with a placeholder parameter. You can customize the parameters as needed.
- **DAX Cluster**: A DAX cluster named `dax-cluster-example` is created with the specified node type and replication factor. It depends on the IAM role, subnet group, and parameter group.

Make sure to replace the placeholder subnet IDs and parameter values with actual values from your environment.

