### Description
The Terraform program defined below fetches the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI using filters. It configures the AWS provider with a default region and does not require any additional input variables.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Default region
}

data "aws_ami" "latest_amazon_linux_2" {
  most_recent = true

  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
  }

  filter {
    name   = "virtualization-type"
    values = ["hvm"]
  }

  owners = ["amazon"]
}

resource "aws_ami" "latest_amazon_linux_2_ami" {
  name              = "latest-amazon-linux-2-ami"
  source_ami_id     = data.aws_ami.latest_amazon_linux_2.id
  source_ami_region = var.region
  virtualization_type = "hvm"

  ebs_block_device {
    device_name = "/dev/sda1"
    volume_size = 8
  }

  timeouts {
    create = "60m"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a default region (`us-west-2`).
- **Data Source**: A `data` resource `aws_ami` is used to fetch the latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI. It uses filters to match the AMI name pattern and virtualization type.
- **Resource**: An `aws_ami` resource is created to create a new AMI based on the fetched latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI. It includes an EBS block device configuration and a timeout setting for the creation process.

