### Description
The Terraform program below creates a DynamoDB table named "ExampleTableName" and enables contributor insights on it. The program ensures that the table exists before attempting to enable contributor insights by establishing a dependency between the two resources.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Default region, can be changed as needed
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name           = "ExampleTableName"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "id"

  attribute {
    name = "id"
    type = "S"
  }
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights" "example_contributor_insights" {
  table_name = aws_dynamodb_table.example_table.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Configures the AWS provider with a default region (`us-west-2`).
2. Creates a DynamoDB table named "ExampleTableName" with a simple hash key (`id`) and uses on-demand billing mode.
3. Enables contributor insights on the created DynamoDB table by referencing its name.

