### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) cluster. It includes the necessary IAM role and parameter group required by the DAX cluster. The IAM role is configured with a trust policy that allows DAX to assume the role, and the parameter group is set up with default parameters.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "dax_role" {
  name = "dax-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "dax.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonDAXFullAccess"
  ]
}

resource "aws_dax_parameter_group" "dax_param_group" {
  name = "dax-param-group"

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_read_throughput_percent"
    value = "100"
  }

  parameters {
    name  = "dax_write_throughput_percent"
    value = "100"
  }
}

resource "aws_dax_cluster" "dax_cluster_example" {
  cluster_name       = "dax-cluster-example"
  iam_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.dax_role.arn
  node_type          = "dax.t3.small"
  replication_factor = 1

  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role.dax_role,
    aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_param_group
  ]

  parameter_group_name = aws_dax_parameter_group.dax_param_group.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration sets up a DAX cluster with the following components:
- An IAM role named `dax-role` with the necessary permissions to allow DAX to access DynamoDB.
- A DAX parameter group named `dax-param-group` with default parameters for read and write throughput.
- A DAX cluster named `dax-cluster-example` that uses the IAM role and parameter group.

