### Description
This Terraform program sets up a basic Amazon Lightsail environment consisting of a bucket, a distribution, an instance, and a key pair. The distribution's origin is set to the bucket, ensuring proper dependency relationships. The program includes default values for all required attributes and uses realistic offline-valid AWS values.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_bucket" "lightsail_bucket" {
  bundle_id = "small_1_0"
  name      = "my-lightsail-bucket"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "lightsail_distribution" {
  bundle_id = "small_1_0"
  name      = "my-lightsail-distribution"

  origin {
    name       = aws_lightsail_bucket.lightsail_bucket.name
    region_name = "us-east-1"
  }

  default_cache_behavior {
    behavior = "cache"
  }
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "lightsail_instance" {
  availability_zone = "us-east-1b"
  blueprint_id      = "ubuntu_20_04"
  bundle_id         = "nano_1_0"
  name              = "my-lightsail-instance"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_key_pair" "lightsail_key_pair" {
  name = "my-lightsail-key-pair"
}
```

This configuration creates:
- An AWS Lightsail bucket named `my-lightsail-bucket`.
- A Lightsail distribution named `my-lightsail-distribution` with the bucket as its origin.
- A Lightsail instance named `my-lightsail-instance` running Ubuntu 20.04.
- A Lightsail key pair named `my-lightsail-key-pair`.

All resources are configured with realistic offline-valid AWS values and dependencies are preserved through Terraform references.

