LLM Output #0:
### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an "authenticate-cognito" action. The ALB will listen on port 443 using HTTPS and will authenticate users via Amazon Cognito. The necessary Cognito resources (user pool, user pool client, and user pool domain) need to be created separately and referenced in the listener's default action.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "front_end" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"
  }

  security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]

  tags = {
    Name = "MyALB"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "front_end" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.front_end.arn
  port              = "443"
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08"
  certificate_arn   = "arn:aws:acm:us-west-2:123456789012:certificate/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"

  default_action {
    type = "authenticate-cognito"

    authenticate_cognito {
      user_pool_arn       = "arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-west-2:123456789012:userpool/us-west-2_XXXXXXXXX"
      user_pool_client_id = "XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"
      user_pool_domain    = "mycognitouserpool.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com"
    }
  }
}
```

### Notes
- Replace `"subnet-0123456789abcdef0"` with a valid subnet ID in your VPC.
- Replace `"sg-0123456789abcdef0"` with a valid security group ID that allows HTTPS traffic.
- Replace `"arn:aws:acm:us-west-2:123456789012:certificate/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012"` with the ARN of your ACM SSL certificate.
- Replace `"arn:aws:cognito-idp:us-west-2:123456789012:userpool/us-west-2_XXXXXXXXX"`, `"XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"`, and `"mycognitouserpool.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com"` with your Cognito User Pool ARN, User Pool Client ID, and User Pool Domain respectively. These resources need to be created separately before deploying this configuration.

